// Title: ETW Tampering (disable event tracing / unhook ntdll)
// Sigma ID: 47e406ef-d07a-5647-eade-0748afecd7b6
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Entroprism (Beijing Yijun Foreign Trade Co., Ltd.)
// Date: 2026-11-03 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: T1562
// Tags: detection.threat_hunting
// Description: Detects attempts to tamper with ETW or unhook ntdll to impair event tracing defenses.
// False positives:
//   - legitimate debugging or instrumentation tools
// References:
//   - https://entroprism.net
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/02019c7f616fa2b4879138907ad45880092bf5b9/rules/windows/process_creation/etw_tampering_disable_event_tracing__unhook_ntdll.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains "EtwEventWrite" or ProcessCommandLine contains "ntdll!Etw") or (ProcessCommandLine contains "NtProtectVirtualMemory" or ProcessCommandLine contains "ntdll.dll")
